00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:28.600
but we do have an
explore option, where

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:32.560
you can go in and explore your
data in a visual interface,

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:36.940
select and make a subset of the
data that you'd like to use,

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:40.710
create calculated columns, and
then started visualizing it.

00:12:40.710 --> 00:12:42.590
And for the
visualization, we'd like

00:12:42.590 --> 00:12:46.600
to show this nice dashboard
that was built by ClickInsight.

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:49.940
This is sort of a meta Data
Studio dashboard that shows off

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:53.630
different types of charts in
Data Studio using a Data Studio

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:54.650
dashboard.

00:12:54.650 --> 00:12:58.390
So as you can see here, we
have a big number type chart,

00:12:58.390 --> 00:13:04.280
bullet chart, donut charts,
also pie charts, bar column,

00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:07.940
paired column, stack bar,
line graphs, stacked area,

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:11.300
scatter plots,
maps, and geoplots.

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:13.580
And all of these graphs
are available to use

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:14.240
