00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:21.800
And those numbers will
show up, and you can read

00:14:21.800 --> 00:14:22.925
through the different text.

00:14:22.925 --> 00:14:26.100
And the dashboard will
explain what is happening.

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:28.730
So you can easily use
Data Studio to create

00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:31.830
interactive infographics.

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:37.520
And then we also have this
very nice dashboard that

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:39.560
uses a Community Connector.

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:42.480
This dashboard uses the Google
Fit Community Connector,

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:45.810
and this was created
by Datasaurus-Rex.

00:14:45.810 --> 00:14:49.420
And this most likely has some
dummy data populating this,

00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:52.540
but you can copy this dashboard
and use the Google Fit

00:14:52.540 --> 00:14:54.809
Community Connector to
populate this using your data.

00:14:54.809 --> 00:14:56.600
And only you have access
to your dashboard,

00:14:56.600 --> 00:14:58.224
and no one else will
be able to see it.

00:14:58.224 --> 00:15:00.110
In this dashboard,
you can see you

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:03.470
can track average weight
over last two weeks,

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:05.780
average activity
over last 28 days,

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:08.900
and average steps taken
over last 28 days.

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:10.580
And this gives you
a nice overview

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:13.810
of what is happening
in your life.

00:15:13.810 --> 00:15:20.220
And lastly, we have this other
example which shows IoT data.

00:15:20.220 --> 00:15:25.490
This is pulling in data
from a BigQuery database,

00:15:25.490 --> 00:15:29.630
and it is pulling in data
for different sensors.

00:15:29.630 --> 00:15:33.410
If you have IoT data maybe in
BigQuery, maybe in Cloud SQL,

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:35.180
or maybe in some
other sources, you

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:39.290
can pull those in and visualize
those IoT data in Data Studio

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:42.420
and share the results
with other people.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:46.140
Now, you have
connected to your data.

00:15:46.140 --> 00:15:47.670
You have visualized it.

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:49.920
But maybe when you're
visualizing it,

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:52.590
you're missing some specific
type of visualization,

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:55.330
or the visualizations that
are available in Data Studio

00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:57.020
doesn't necessarily
work for you.

00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:59.520
For that, we have a new feature
that is in Developer Preview

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:02.130
right now that is
called Community Vis.

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:04.680
What this lets you do is
build your own visualization

00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:08.370
in JavaScript, and then you can
bring that into Data Studio.

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:11.370
And we have the documentation
available in our developer

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:12.880
site.

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:15.310
It will tell you how you can
build your own visualization.

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:18.780
And we'll also take a
look at a live example.

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:20.700
Let's have a look
at the showcase

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:23.940
and see what different
examples we have.

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:29.150
So let's say we'll look at
this Sunburst dashboard.

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:33.470
So Matt, if someone is trying
to build a visualization--

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:37.010
if they already know D3 and
already can build a base,

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:40.320
how much difficult is it
to bring that visualization

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:41.210
into Data Studio?

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:41.870
MATT HAMRICK: I would
say if you're already

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:43.786
familiar with the
visualization library you're

00:16:43.786 --> 00:16:46.280
looking to use, it's probably
35, 45 minutes for this one.

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:47.420
It's a little bit simpler.

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:49.320
MINHAZ KAZI: OK, that's
very interesting.

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:51.789
So maybe we'll have more
of our audience bringing

00:16:51.789 --> 00:16:53.080
visualizations for Data Studio.

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:54.080
MATT HAMRICK: Let's
hope for that too.

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:55.580
MINHAZ KAZI: So as
you can see, this

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:59.520
is a JavaScript-based
visualization built in D3,

00:16:59.520 --> 00:17:02.330
and that's being visualized
in Data Studio right now.

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:06.200
And it'll work with other Data
Studio functions, like filters.

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:10.256
If you are using dropdowns,
all that will work with this.

00:17:10.256 --> 00:17:11.880
This is right now in
Developer Preview.

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:13.254
So if you'd like
to use this, you

00:17:13.254 --> 00:17:15.089
can go to our developer
site and sign up

00:17:15.089 --> 00:17:16.172
for the developer preview.

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:21.710
So you've collected your
data, you've analyzed it,

00:17:21.710 --> 00:17:23.030
and you have visualized it.

00:17:23.030 --> 00:17:24.734
But now, you'd
like to share this.

00:17:24.734 --> 00:17:26.150
There are different
sharing models

00:17:26.150 --> 00:17:28.220
available in Data Studio.

00:17:28.220 --> 00:17:31.880
So first of all, you can share
the reports using the G Suite

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:34.100
or Drive permissions, so
just the same way you'd

00:17:34.100 --> 00:17:38.280
share Docs, Slides, you
can similarly share reports

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:39.030
with other people.

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:42.410
You can share them by user
or across your organization,

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:43.460
or anyone with a link.

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:47.450
And you can also give people
View access or Edit access.

00:17:47.450 --> 00:17:49.280
If you give someone
View access, they'll

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:51.140
only be able to view the
dashboard and [? pair them ?]

00:17:51.140 --> 00:17:52.598
with the controls
on the dashboard,

00:17:52.598 --> 00:17:55.670
but they won't be able to change
anything in the dashboard.

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:57.650
But if you give
them Edit access,

00:17:57.650 --> 00:18:00.350
they can use the data sources
available in the dashboard

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:04.404
and create new
charts and graphs.

00:18:04.404 --> 00:18:05.820
Now, there's a
separate data model

00:18:05.820 --> 00:18:07.730
available for data
sources that you add.

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:09.960
As you remember,
data sources are

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:13.740
when you use connectors to
connect to specific datasets,

00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:17.350
those are added as data
sources in Data Studio.

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:19.700
Data sources can also
be shared with users.

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:21.620
Data sources can have
Viewer's credentials

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:23.150
or Owner's credentials.

00:18:23.150 --> 00:18:27.070
What that means is if you create
a data source with Owner's

00:18:27.070 --> 00:18:30.110
credentials and you
create the data source

00:18:30.110 --> 00:18:33.080
and then you add the data
source to a dashboard, anyone

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:35.887
who views that dashboard
will see your data.

00:18:35.887 --> 00:18:37.470
However, if you
create the data source

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:40.000
with Viewer's credentials and
then you create a dashboard

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:42.080
with that, whoever is
viewing the dashboard

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:43.560
will see their data.

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:46.050
An example of this would be
Google Analytics dashboard,

00:18:46.050 --> 00:18:47.990
where if you put in
Viewer's credentials,

00:18:47.990 --> 00:18:49.280
it'll be the same dashboard.

00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:51.680
But when you view it, you
will see your accounts,

00:18:51.680 --> 00:18:53.690
but when someone
else views that,

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:56.660
they'll see their accounts
in the same dashboard.

00:18:56.660 --> 00:18:59.220
Data sources can also be
shared with View access

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:02.028
or Edit access.

00:19:02.028 --> 00:19:03.730
And when you create
a dashboard, you

00:19:03.730 --> 00:19:06.530
can also embed it as a
report or infographic

00:19:06.530 --> 00:19:08.270
on different websites.

00:19:08.270 --> 00:19:10.310
We currently support
iFrame-based embeds

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:11.540
and also oEmbed.

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:14.480
Let's see two examples.

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:19.790
This first one is, I believe,
a blog post on the Google Cloud

00:19:19.790 --> 00:19:21.800
Big Data blog, where
there was a-- we

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:26.000
made a blog post on the bitcoin
blockchain data in BigQuery.

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:28.730
And as you can see here,
this is a normal blog post,

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:30.960
but this dashboard is an
interactive Data Studio

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:34.590
dashboard that has been
embedded using iFrame.

00:19:34.590 --> 00:19:38.940
And this second link that
we have is another blog

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:42.280
post made on Medium by
one of the developer

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:43.740
advocates at Google.

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:48.890
And this dashboard over here
visualizes all the FIFA World

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:49.860
Cup goals so far.

00:19:49.860 --> 00:19:51.443
And you can play
around with the data.

00:19:51.443 --> 00:19:52.770
You can filter it.

00:19:52.770 --> 00:19:55.560
It also changes the links
based on your selection.

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:57.689
And you can view
details on demand

00:19:57.689 --> 00:19:59.355
as you hover over
different data points.

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:04.440
So once you've
built a dashboard,

00:20:04.440 --> 00:20:07.030
you can also use it
as a presentation.

00:20:07.030 --> 00:20:10.010
Instead of using a slide, if
you're giving a presentation

00:20:10.010 --> 00:20:13.000
and if you want to show it
as you're presenting it,

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:14.900
you can show the
dashboard full screen

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:20.080
and play around with it,
use different filters.

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:22.570
Also, in Data Studio, you can
use the Community Connectors

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:24.820
to build push button solutions.

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:28.000
What that means is maybe the
users you are trying to reach

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:29.170
do not know SQL.

00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:32.296
Maybe they don't know about
the database that you're using.

00:20:32.296 --> 00:20:33.670
Maybe they don't
know the schema.

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:36.530
Maybe they don't even know
how to use Data Studio,

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:38.170
or they have a
constraint of time.

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:39.880
What they would
like to do is they'd

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:41.380
like to connect to
your data source,

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:44.410
provide some configuration,
view their data,

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:47.180
and then have a
templated result.

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:50.590
So you can do that using
Community Connectors.

00:20:50.590 --> 00:20:53.110
What you can do is you can
create a Community Connector.

00:20:53.110 --> 00:20:54.890
You can attach a template to it.

00:20:54.890 --> 00:20:56.556
And once the template
has been attached,

00:20:56.556 --> 00:20:59.500
you can deploy the Community
Connector using a single link.

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:01.420
And what will happen
then is your user

00:21:01.420 --> 00:21:06.472
will come in, click on that
link, view the configuration.

00:21:06.472 --> 00:21:08.680
And they'll fill in the
configuration, click Connect,

00:21:08.680 --> 00:21:12.130
and they'll see a templated
dashboard with their data.

00:21:12.130 --> 00:21:15.010
And that dashboard will
be created only for them,

00:21:15.010 --> 00:21:16.311
and they'll be able to edit it.

00:21:16.311 --> 00:21:18.310
They can share it if they
want, or they can just

00:21:18.310 --> 00:21:19.960
view it for themselves.

00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:22.660
Let's see an example
of what we mean.

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:26.710
So this is a dataset
available in BigQuery.

00:21:26.710 --> 00:21:28.410
This is a Chrome User
Experience Report

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:32.540
that has data for over five
million different URLs.

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:35.250
And it will contain
data about timing

00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:37.650
for First Paint, First
Contentful Paint,

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:39.452
DOMContentLoaded, and onload.

00:21:39.452 --> 00:21:41.160
And it will show the
distribution of time

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:43.020
for all of these websites.

00:21:43.020 --> 00:21:45.690
You can further dig down into
the data using dimensions

00:21:45.690 --> 00:21:50.190
like Effective Connection Type,
like 4G, 3G; device type--

00:21:50.190 --> 00:21:52.350
phone, tablet, or
desktop; or which country

00:21:52.350 --> 00:21:54.830
the users are coming from.

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:57.560
So all of this data is
available in BigQuery.

00:21:57.560 --> 00:21:59.700
If you Google the BigQuery
site for this dashboard,

00:21:59.700 --> 00:22:02.320
you can see that this data
is kept there by month.

00:22:02.320 --> 00:22:04.520
Now, if anyone wants
to access this data,

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:08.810
they'll have to go into
BigQuery, create their own SQL,

00:22:08.810 --> 00:22:09.800
and then run the SQL.

00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:11.425
And then they can
access the data.

00:22:11.425 --> 00:22:12.800
And if they want
to visualize it,

00:22:12.800 --> 00:22:15.258
they can bring the data into
Data Studio using the BigQuery

00:22:15.258 --> 00:22:16.610
connector.

00:22:16.610 --> 00:22:18.350
That is the more
longer way and if you

00:22:18.350 --> 00:22:19.740
want to get finer control.

00:22:19.740 --> 00:22:22.080
But if you're, let's say,
the owner of this data,

00:22:22.080 --> 00:22:26.180
and if you want to give a more
easier solution to your users,

00:22:26.180 --> 00:22:29.330
what you can do is create
a Community Connector.

00:22:29.330 --> 00:22:32.110
And we've done that and
we'll show you the example.

00:22:32.110 --> 00:22:33.860
So after creating the
Community Connector,

00:22:33.860 --> 00:22:37.130
all you give to your users
is just this one URL.

00:22:37.130 --> 00:22:41.810
So we click on this URL, and
we'll go into Data Studio

00:22:41.810 --> 00:22:45.380
with that connector selected
and waiting for configuration.

00:22:45.380 --> 00:22:48.650
And Matt, I believe we can
also use this new feature

00:22:48.650 --> 00:22:50.151
to pre-configure
this configuration.

00:22:50.151 --> 00:22:52.566
MATT HAMRICK: Yes, this would
be able to be pre-configured

00:22:52.566 --> 00:22:53.110
as well.

00:22:53.110 --> 00:22:53.984
MINHAZ KAZI: Awesome.

00:22:53.984 --> 00:22:56.000
So we will add in a URL.

00:22:56.000 --> 00:23:00.160
Let's say we'll
put in Wikipedia.

00:23:00.160 --> 00:23:05.570
And we'll enable this parameter
to be modified in the report.

00:23:05.570 --> 00:23:07.630
So we'll click Connect, Allow.

00:23:10.960 --> 00:23:13.210
And the schema looks fine.

00:23:13.210 --> 00:23:16.210
And we'll click
on Create Report.

00:23:16.210 --> 00:23:19.120
So this will fetch the data
from the BigQuery database

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:20.800
and then create a
live connection.

00:23:20.800 --> 00:23:23.310
And then it will
showcase that data

00:23:23.310 --> 00:23:26.600
in this dashboard that is
created only for my user.

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:28.420
And I can edit this.

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:30.160
I can also share this
with other people.

00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:31.980
And as you can see, we
have different pages

00:23:31.980 --> 00:23:34.480
available for this
dashboard that

00:23:34.480 --> 00:23:37.580
uses the data for Wikipedia.

00:23:37.580 --> 00:23:39.260
Now, we have three
different pages.

00:23:39.260 --> 00:23:40.940
And we can also view it.

00:23:40.940 --> 00:23:45.790
Now, this dashboard is created
only specifically for me,

00:23:45.790 --> 00:23:48.190
so I can go ahead and
edit it and this will not

00:23:48.190 --> 00:23:49.510
edit the template.

00:23:49.510 --> 00:23:52.720
So I can go into the
first page, and maybe

00:23:52.720 --> 00:23:56.302
I also want to see this
data for a separate website.

00:23:56.302 --> 00:23:58.510
So as you can see, this is
a completely drag-and-drop

00:23:58.510 --> 00:24:02.850
interface where I can
make any kind of changes.

00:24:02.850 --> 00:24:07.750
I will move this
one to the left.

00:24:07.750 --> 00:24:12.050
And we'll try to quickly make
some new changes to this.

00:24:12.050 --> 00:24:14.127
So rotate this.

00:24:14.127 --> 00:24:15.960
We'll pick all the
elements on the dashboard

00:24:15.960 --> 00:24:17.190
that can be configured.

00:24:17.190 --> 00:24:18.984
We'll copy-paste them.

00:24:18.984 --> 00:24:21.340
We'll move them to the side.

00:24:21.340 --> 00:24:25.710
And let's say we will
change the parameter

00:24:25.710 --> 00:24:27.720
to have a different website.

00:24:27.720 --> 00:24:31.104
So maybe we'll
look at Google.com.

00:24:34.240 --> 00:24:36.880
So as you can see,
this is completely

00:24:36.880 --> 00:24:38.130
configurable by the dashboard.

00:24:38.130 --> 00:24:39.930
And as we type in the
new configuration,

00:24:39.930 --> 00:24:41.610
we have this
side-by-side comparison

00:24:41.610 --> 00:24:44.800
for the website performance
of these two websites.

00:24:44.800 --> 00:24:46.650
And once I've done
that, I can go in

00:24:46.650 --> 00:24:48.900
and I can share this
report with other people.

00:24:48.900 --> 00:24:51.340
I can share this by link and
publish this on a website.

00:24:51.340 --> 00:24:54.240
I can share this with specific
people within my organization.

00:24:54.240 --> 00:24:58.410
Or I can even share this
across my organization.

00:24:58.410 --> 00:25:00.710
But this is how you can build
a completely push button

00:25:00.710 --> 00:25:05.090
solution using Community
Connectors in Data Studio.

00:25:05.090 --> 00:25:08.630
So to recap, Data Studio
is Google's free business

00:25:08.630 --> 00:25:10.260
intelligence and
reporting platform.

00:25:10.260 --> 00:25:12.370
And you can connect
to any data source

00:25:12.370 --> 00:25:15.209
and make any visualization
that you want in Data Studio.

00:25:15.209 --> 00:25:16.750
And you can share
your visualizations

00:25:16.750 --> 00:25:19.790
with others in different ways.

00:25:19.790 --> 00:25:23.310
If you are trying to know
more about Data Studio,

00:25:23.310 --> 00:25:24.880
you can build a
dashboard by going

00:25:24.880 --> 00:25:27.840
into datastudio.google.com.

00:25:27.840 --> 00:25:32.140
If you want to see more examples
of dashboards built in Data

00:25:32.140 --> 00:25:35.480
Studio, you can go to
datastudio.google.com/gallery.

00:25:35.480 --> 00:25:41.700
This has templates from our
users and different partners.

00:25:41.700 --> 00:25:44.640
You can also have a look at
the Community Connector gallery

00:25:44.640 --> 00:25:48.240
by going to
datastudio.google.com/data.

00:25:48.240 --> 00:25:52.050
You can get support by going to
support.google.com/datastudio.

00:25:52.050 --> 00:25:54.957
If you're more into
developing solutions,

00:25:54.957 --> 00:25:56.790
maybe Community Connectors
or Community Vis,

00:25:56.790 --> 00:25:58.248
you can go into
our developer site,

00:25:58.248 --> 00:25:59.835
which is available
at developers.googl

00:25:59.835 --> 00:26:01.500
e.com/datastudio.

00:26:01.500 --> 00:26:04.140
We also have an open source
repository available which has

00:26:04.140 --> 00:26:07.900
examples of different code,
and you can go there by going

00:26:07.900 --> 00:26:10.380
to github.com/googledatastudio.

00:26:10.380 --> 00:26:13.380
If you build something cool--
maybe an awesome dashboard,

00:26:13.380 --> 00:26:15.030
maybe a connector, maybe a vis--

00:26:15.030 --> 00:26:19.350
share that with us by using
the hashtag #googledatastudio.

00:26:19.350 --> 00:26:21.821
And now, stay tuned
for live Q&amp;A. We'll

00:26:21.821 --> 00:26:23.070
be back in less than a minute.

00:28:17.450 --> 00:28:19.000
Welcome back to the Q&amp;A session.

00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:22.070
Looks like we have a few
questions from our audience.

00:28:22.070 --> 00:28:25.990
So the first question is, can
we integrate graphs and reports

00:28:25.990 --> 00:28:30.180
created using Data Studio
directly with Web Applications?

00:28:30.180 --> 00:28:32.590
And it also us about
real-time reports.

00:28:32.590 --> 00:28:33.580
MATT HAMRICK: I'll go
ahead and take this one.

00:28:33.580 --> 00:28:34.090
MINHAZ KAZI: Sure.

00:28:34.090 --> 00:28:36.040
MATT HAMRICK: So we can
integrate graphs and reports

00:28:36.040 --> 00:28:37.690
in Data Studio directly
in the Web Apps.

00:28:37.690 --> 00:28:39.565
We kind of showed off
a few examples of that.

00:28:39.565 --> 00:28:42.400
There was the blog post
that Minhaz showed.

00:28:42.400 --> 00:28:44.404
Those links should
be available as well.

00:28:44.404 --> 00:28:45.820
Real-time reports
